# Plain-English Custom Rule Authoring Guide

Whenever the user states a custom rule, preference, constraint, or requirement in plain English (e.g., *"I don't want any jQuery"*, *"Never use localStorage"*, *"Always require phone number in forms"*), the AI Agent MUST automatically perform the following 3 steps:

---

## 1. Create AI Rule File
Create a new rule file in `.cursor/rules/custom-<topic>.mdc` and `.agents/rules/custom-<topic>.md`:

```yaml
---
description: <Short explanation of user preference>
alwaysApply: true
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
---

# <Rule Title>
- User Requirement: <Exact quote from user>
- Strictly forbidden / required patterns.
```

---

## 2. Register into `custom-rules.json`
Append the rule into `custom-rules.json` so `pnpm run audit:rules` and Git pre-commit hooks automatically check it:

```json
{
  "name": "no-jquery",
  "type": "forbidden",
  "pattern": "(\\$|jQuery)\\(",
  "scope": "src",
  "description": "No jQuery usage (user preference)",
  "message": "Direct jQuery call detected. Use standard React state/DOM.",
  "severity": "critical"
}
```

---

## 3. Confirm to User
Confirm in concise terms:
> *"✔ Custom rule recorded from plain English. Enforced across AI generation, `pnpm run audit:rules`, and Git pre-commit."*
